cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  This is public-domain model legislation, released under CC0 1.0. Please cite
  the publication version and commit so readers can identify the text reviewed.
title: "Frontier Artificial Intelligence Responsible Officer Act"
abstract: >-
  Sponsor-facing model state legislation applying the responsible corporate
  officer doctrine of United States v. Dotterweich and United States v. Park to
  covered frontier artificial-intelligence systems. The draft assigns personal,
  non-delegable duties to natural persons with final material independent
  decision authority and practical power over covered conduct. Coverage begins
  at a 10^26-operation training-and-lineage threshold or prospective capability
  designation and is limited by an adopting-state nexus. The base individual
  offense requires failure to exercise due care. Separate entity liability does
  not satisfy individual liability, and the draft restricts corporate insurance,
  indemnification, reimbursement, or offset of individual sanctions. Public-domain
  research draft; never introduced or enacted; no completed review claimed.
